"<div><div class=\" response-message\"></div></div><h2>Resource System Design</h2>\n<p>✅ Design complete</p>\n<p>This design for <strong>Galactic Trader</strong> focuses on a &quot;Logistics Strategy&quot; model. Despite the title, the &quot;Trading&quot; aspect is thematic—players act as a solo blockade runner or fleet commander who must manage internal logistics to progress through a linear series of increasingly dangerous star sectors.</p>\n<hr />\n<h3>1. Resource Identity: Titanium Alloy (Material)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Type</strong>: Primary Construction Material.</li>\n<li><strong>Purpose</strong>: The physical backbone of the game. It is used for crafting ship modules, repairing hull damage, and building station infrastructure.</li>\n<li><strong>Thematic Fit</strong>: Represents the raw physical mass required to survive in space. It grounds the player in the &quot;industrial&quot; side of space strategy.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2. Resource Identity: Ion Cells (Currency/Energy)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Type</strong>: Operational Currency.</li>\n<li><strong>Purpose</strong>: Acts as both &quot;fuel&quot; for movement and the medium of exchange for automated services (refueling, hiring NPC escorts, or activating jump gates).</li>\n<li><strong>Thematic Fit</strong>: Represents the power required to keep systems running. In a world without open trading, energy is the only universal constant of value.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>3. Resource Identity: Neural Data (Experience/Progression)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Type</strong>: Progression Resource (XP).</li>\n<li><strong>Purpose</strong>: Used to unlock new blueprints in the Tech Tree and &quot;level up&quot; the player’s command capabilities. It represents the &quot;linear&quot; gatekeeper of the game.</li>\n<li><strong>Thematic Fit</strong>: Represents the mapping of the galaxy and the reverse-engineering of alien tech.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>4. Resource Identity: Void Shards (Premium/Catalyst)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Type</strong>: Rare Catalyst / Premium Resource.</li>\n<li><strong>Purpose</strong>: Used to bypass crafting timers, guarantee &quot;Masterwork&quot; rolls on gear, or purchase unique cosmetic ship hulls. It can also be used to &quot;overclock&quot; production for a limited time.</li>\n<li><strong>Thematic Fit</strong>: A mysterious substance found only in the hearts of collapsed stars, allowing for the manipulation of space-time.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h3>Generation Sources</h3>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr><th align=\"left\">Resource</th><th align=\"left\">Primary Source</th><th align=\"left\">Amount</th><th align=\"left\">Frequency</th><th align=\"left\">Scaling</th></tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Titanium Alloy</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Asteroid Mining / Salvaging Wrecks</td><td align=\"left\">50–200 per node</td><td align=\"left\">High (Every mission)</td><td align=\"left\">Node richness increases in later sectors.</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Ion Cells</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Solar Harvesting / Mission Rewards</td><td align=\"left\">10–50 per minute</td><td align=\"left\">Constant (Passive/Active)</td><td align=\"left\">Better &quot;Solar Sails&quot; increase passive gain.</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Neural Data</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Scanning Anomalies / Combat Victory</td><td align=\"left\">5–20 per scan</td><td align=\"left\">Medium (Exploration)</td><td align=\"left\">Higher-tier enemies drop more complex data.</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Void Shards</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Boss Encounters / Daily Login / IAP</td><td align=\"left\">1–5 per event</td><td align=\"left\">Very Low (Milestones)</td><td align=\"left\">Fixed; does not scale to prevent inflation.</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h3>Consumption Uses</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Titanium Alloy</strong>:\n<ul>\n<li><em>Crafting</em>: 500–5,000 per module.</li>\n<li><em>Repairs</em>: 10 per 1% Hull HP.</li>\n<li><em>Value</em>: Essential for survival; without it, the player cannot upgrade their stats to face harder sectors.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Ion Cells</strong>:\n<ul>\n<li><em>Travel</em>: 50 per Sector Jump.</li>\n<li><em>Refining</em>: 100 per batch of Alloy processed.</li>\n<li><em>Value</em>: The &quot;Action Point&quot; equivalent. It dictates how much the player can do in a single session.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Neural Data</strong>:\n<ul>\n<li><em>Tech Tree</em>: 100–10,000 per node.</li>\n<li><em>Value</em>: The only way to unlock the next tier of equipment. It drives the linear progression.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Void Shards</strong>:\n<ul>\n<li><em>Speed-up</em>: 10 per hour of crafting skipped.</li>\n<li><em>Quality</em>: 50 to ensure a &quot;Legendary&quot; craft.</li>\n<li><em>Value</em>: Convenience and &quot;Min-Maxing&quot; for end-game players.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h3>Storage and Limits</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Titanium Alloy</strong>: Limited by <strong>Cargo Bay Capacity</strong>.\n<ul>\n<li><em>Rationale</em>: Forces players to choose between carrying raw materials or finished goods.</li>\n<li><em>Overflow</em>: Excess is jettisoned (lost) unless the player builds &quot;Storage Depots.&quot;</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Ion Cells</strong>: Limited by <strong>Battery Capacity</strong>.\n<ul>\n<li><em>Rationale</em>: Prevents infinite kiting/traveling. Players must return to &quot;Sun Zones&quot; to recharge.</li>\n<li><em>Overflow</em>: Wasted as heat (no benefit).</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Neural Data</strong>: <strong>Unlimited</strong>.\n<ul>\n<li><em>Rationale</em>: As a progression resource, capping it feels punitive and discourages exploration.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Void Shards</strong>: <strong>Unlimited</strong>.\n<ul>\n<li><em>Rationale</em>: Standard for premium resources to ensure players never lose what they purchase.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h3>Exchange Rates (Internal Conversion)</h3>\n<p><em>Since Trading is disabled, these are fixed &quot;Alchemy&quot; or &quot;Refinery&quot; rates:</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Refining</strong>: 2x Raw Ore + 10 Ion Cells $\\rightarrow$ 1 Titanium Alloy.</li>\n<li><strong>Data Extraction</strong>: 100 Titanium Alloy (Scrapped) $\\rightarrow$ 5 Neural Data.</li>\n<li><strong>Emergency Power</strong>: 1 Void Shard $\\rightarrow$ 1,000 Ion Cells (Instant refill).</li>\n<li><strong>Market Dynamics</strong>: There is no fluctuating market. Instead, &quot;Sector Difficulty&quot; acts as a tax; as players move to higher sectors, the Ion Cell cost for travel increases, requiring more efficient crafting.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h3>Sink Mechanisms &amp; Balance</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>The Repair Sink (Titanium)</strong>: As enemies get stronger, the &quot;Titanium Tax&quot; for repairing the ship increases. This prevents players from hoarding infinite Alloy.</li>\n<li><strong>The Jump Tax (Ion Cells)</strong>: Moving between sectors consumes Ion Cells. If a player stalls in a sector too long, they may run out of energy, forcing them to &quot;Scrap&quot; modules to generate emergency power.</li>\n<li><strong>The Tech Ceiling (Neural Data)</strong>: Each new tier of technology costs exponentially more Data. This ensures players cannot skip the linear progression of the game.</li>\n<li><strong>Inflation Prevention</strong>: Because there is no player-to-player trading, inflation is impossible. The economy is a closed loop between the player and the environment. The &quot;Sink&quot; is the linear progression itself—old resources become obsolete as the player moves to higher-tier materials (e.g., Titanium Alloy Grade 2).</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Meaningful Choices</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Short-term vs. Long-term</strong>: Do I spend my Ion Cells to mine more Titanium (Short-term survival) or use them to scan anomalies for Neural Data (Long-term progression)?</li>\n<li><strong>Inventory Management</strong>: My Cargo Bay is full. Do I keep the Titanium to repair my ship later, or do I scrap it for Neural Data to unlock a better shield blueprint now?</li>\n<li><strong>Progression Paths</strong>: Players can focus on &quot;Industrial&quot; upgrades (increasing storage/mining) or &quot;Combat&quot; upgrades (increasing data gain from kills), allowing for different playstyles within the linear path.</li>\n</ul>\n<div><div class=\" completion-message response-message\"></div></div>"